{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nDiscovered while confirming the root cause of `enchanting-phantastic-weevil`\n(a61d-adf9-3725-4847). Independent of that ticket's scheme-downgrade concern, and deliberately\nleft out of its scope.\n\n`location /review/` proxies with a prefix-STRIPPING form\n(`proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}/;`, `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`), so the\nreview-bot app never sees the `/review/` prefix. When the app emits an ABSOLUTE redirect it builds\nit from the public `Host` header, so the emitted path has no `/review/` prefix to strip — and the\nprefix is simply lost.\n\n## Observed (deployed edge, unauthenticated)\n\n    GET https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/review/health/\n      -> HTTP/2 307, location: http://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/health\n\nThe correct target is `…/review/health`. `…/health` matches no review-bot location, falls through\nto `location /` -> Gerrit, and 404s. Same for `/review/webhook/` and `/review/rerun/`.\n\n## Root cause (PROVEN — see RCA comment)\n\nPost-a61d the app emits `https://$host/<route>` (correct scheme, no `/review/`). None of a61d's\nthree rules match a `https://$host/...` Location (they match `http://…` prefixes + the loopback\ndefault), so the prefix is lost. Confirmed on real nginx (1.27-alpine) + a stub upstream emitting\nthe Starlette-style absolute redirect: current block loses the prefix, block + the one new rule\nrestores it, and both leave the prefix-stripping REQUEST path (`GET /review/health` -> app\n`/health`) unchanged.\n\nReview-bot redirect surface is same-app-only: `uvicorn rebar.review_bot.app:app`, plain\n`FastAPI(...)` (no `root_path`, no `redirect_slashes`), no `RedirectResponse`, no `--root-path`,\nroutes `/health` `/webhook` `/rerun`. So the broad same-host rewrite has no legitimate off-`/review/`\nredirect to corrupt today.\n\n## Chosen approach (Option 1 — operator-approved, verified)\n\nEdge fix only. Add ONE per-location rule to the `/review/` block, AFTER a61d's scheme backstops\n(the restated `proxy_redirect default;` stays FIRST):\n\n    proxy_redirect https://$host/ https://$host/review/;\n\nnginx applies the first matching `proxy_redirect`; the new rule's `https://$host/` prefix overlaps\nnone of the existing rules (they match `http://…`), so it neither shadows nor is shadowed by them.\na61d's scheme guarantee (http->https) and the prefix-stripping request path are both preserved.\nOption 2 (app-side `root_path`/APIRouter mount) is REJECTED (operator decision 2026-08-30).\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n1. `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`, `/review/` block: append the one `proxy_redirect\n   https://$host/ https://$host/review/;` rule after the two a61d scheme rules; add a guard comment\n   documenting the same-app-only precondition + the residual.\n2. Confirm the RENDERED config still passes `nginx -t` in a throwaway `nginx:1.27-alpine` container.\n\n## Test plan (`tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py`, reuse a61d's `_render_nginx()` / `_location_body()`)\n\n- (1) `/review/` block restores the prefix: a `proxy_redirect https://$host/ https://$host/review/;`\n  rule is present.\n- (2) request path unchanged: `/review/` still `proxy_pass …/;` (prefix-stripping) — no accidental\n  break of the app's `/health` mapping.\n- (3) a61d scheme guarantee still holds on `/review/` (no regression of the http->https rules or the\n  `default`-first ordering).\n- (4) ordering: the prefix-restore rule appears AFTER `default` (default first).\n- (5) residual guard: pin the review-bot redirect surface as same-app-only over\n  `src/rebar/review_bot/` (no `RedirectResponse`, no `root_path`/`--root-path`), so a future\n  off-`/review/` absolute redirect that the broad rewrite would mis-prefix is caught.\n\nStructural tests run in-process (no CI provider dependency) — portable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] It is established which absolute URLs the review-bot app can emit (same-app-only; RCA comment).\n- [ ] A request to `https://<host>/review/<route>/` receives a `Location` retaining the `/review/`\n      prefix, verified by a structural test over the rendered nginx config.\n- [ ] The existing prefix-stripping request behaviour is unchanged: `GET /review/health` still\n      reaches the app as `GET /health`.\n- [ ] LIVE VALIDATION (DEFERRED to operator edge-deploy): an unauthenticated probe of\n      `/review/health/` on the deployed edge shows a `Location` resolving to the health endpoint.\n      Satisfied by the SAME operator edge-deploy that clears a61d's AC5 (gated on bug 1d1b +\n      operator apply). Not deployed here; not blocking.\n\n## Defect attribution\n\ncaused_by **786b-190d-5e3a-4194** (smelly-pane-bolt, \"infra: S2 — deploy Gerrit + review-bot behind\nnginx/TLS\"); commit `6cd6f4e1f7c0` created the `/review/` block + prefix-stripping proxy_pass in one\nnew-file commit; the prefix loss was latent from creation -> close-class **preexisting**.\n\n## Notes\n\nReported from unauthenticated probes and repo inspection only. No credential was transmitted."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788111348012943300,"uuid":"cfed79a9-6d9d-427f-b4c1-ed4a099adbb4"}